==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|frm|en}} {{term|eligible|lang=frm}} from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|eligibilis|lang=la}} from {{term|eligo|ēligō|select, choose|lang=la}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# [[suitable]]; meeting the [[condition]]s; [[worthy]] of being [[chosen]]

====Usage notes====
Used in the phrase ''{{w|eligible bachelor}}'' to mean “desirable male”, the corresponding term for a woman is {{term|nubile|lang=en}}.

====Antonyms====
* [[ineligible]]

